    "description": {
      "value": "The serrated blade of this +1 striking dagger has a greenish tinge, and the hilt is sculpted to look like the head of a serpent about to strike. When you critically succeed at an attack roll with the dagger of venom, the target becomes sickened 1 unless it succeeds at a DC 19 Fortitude save. This is a poison effect. In addition, you can activate the dagger to poison a creature with a more potent poison.\n\nActivate (Free Action)\nFrequency: once per day\nYou poison the creature you hit with dagger venom.\n\n**Dagger Venom**\nDC: 21\nSaving Throw: Fortitude\nMaximum Duration: 4 rounds\n- Stage 1: 1d8 poison damage and enfeebled 1."
    },
